<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii)",
        "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That the three saturated spots are a measured cribral lattice, that 284.76 nm equals 242 nm, or that the gallery spiral was predicted ab initio.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3118 coefficients a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 chosen so the analytic fastest mode equals the assigned 242 nm detail scale on a 6-wavelength Neumann patch. A 3-arm logarithmic spiral biases the initial condition. The GIF is the unguided activator passed through the gallery photograph's colour quantiles.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species mass-action system du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v has a stable homogeneous fixed point that can be Turing-unstable.",
        "reported_in_source: Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008: diatom biosilica nanopatterns are consistent with polyamine phase separation inside the silica deposition vesicle.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator.",
        "reported_in_source: Yendo & Akatsuka 1910: Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii was observed alive forming auxospores, so the species is extant (Holocene, 0 Ma).",
        "transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the campaign detail-scale assignment (tier 2_macromolecular_100nm), not a pore spacing measured on A. ehrenbergii in the cited papers.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery JPEG is a stylized 100 μm frame, about 413 times coarser than 242 nm. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp., not a confirmed ehrenbergii type." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Arachnoidiscus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/arachnoidiscus_ehrenbergii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species mass-action system du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v has a stable homogeneous fixed point that can be Turing-unstable. | Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008: diatom biosilica nanopatterns are consistent with polyamine phase separation inside the silica deposition vesicle. | Yendo & Akatsuka 1910: Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii was observed alive forming auxospores, so the species is extant (Holocene, 0 Ma).; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3118 coefficients a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 chosen so the analytic fastest mode equals the assigned 242 nm detail scale on a 6-wavelength Neumann patch. A 3-arm logarithmic spiral biases the initial condition. The GIF is the unguided activator passed through the gallery photograph's colour quantiles.; transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the campaign detail-scale assignment (tier 2_macromolecular_100nm), not a pore spacing measured on A. ehrenbergii in the cited papers. | The gallery JPEG is a stylized 100 μm frame, about 413 times coarser than 242 nm. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp., not a confirmed ehrenbergii type.; does_not_claim: That the three saturated spots are a measured cribral lattice, that 284.76 nm equals 242 nm, or that the gallery spiral was predicted ab initio.]; phenomenon_size: 144 nm (1.44e-07 m, log10=-6.842 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 144 nm to 450 µm): 144 nm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-bioelectric-polarity, 538 nm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-vertex-packing, 10 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength, 19 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-clock-wavefront, 43 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-elastic-buckling, 58 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-morphogen-condensation, 76 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-flux-canalization, 100 µm:arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-branching-tree" ;
